# What Docker may copy into a build (the build context). Everything stays out unless
# listed below, so a new private file (notes, secrets, a local script) never ends up in
# an image. Docker does not read .gitignore.
*

# What the Dockerfile copies:
!web/
!shared/
!server/pyproject.toml
!server/app/
!server/alembic.ini
!server/migrations/
!docker/start.sh

# ...and within those, never these. The order matters: the last matching line wins.
# node_modules and dist are built inside the image, for Linux.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
**/__pycache__/
**/.env*
